    "report": "Archiving is implemented and committed on a new branch, `messaging-archive-conversation`, not pushed. The full test suite, typecheck, lint, format check and `check:conventions` all pass.\n\n**Branch:** you said to commit on the current branch, but that was `main`, and the harness rule is to branch first when on the default branch. So the commit (`98358e3`) sits on the new branch, and `main` still ends at the previous developer's WIP commit. Merge or fast-forward it if you want it on `main`.\n\n**What was already there:** the previous developer's commit had the domain behaviour (`archiveFor`, `isArchivedBy`, the event, snapshot support), the archive table and its persistence, the command handler, and a domain spec. I kept all of it.\n\n**What I added:**\n- **List and unread:** the summary now carries an `archived` flag, computed in SQL against the reader's archive row and the conversation's last message. `GET /conversations/mine` leaves archived conversations out and strips the flag, so its response shape is unchanged. `GET /conversations/unread` still counts them.\n- **Route and wiring:** `POST /conversations/:id/archive`, answered with 202 like `/read`, and the command registered once in the Messaging module.\n- **Tests:** a new `conversationArchives.routes.e2e.spec.ts` with 6 cases covering the list, unread counts, the comeback on a new message from either side, re-archiving, refusal to a stranger or an unknown id, and refusal when not signed in.\n\n**Choices I made where the request was open:**\n- \"Last message\" includes messages hidden by an upheld report, because the aggregate counts them. So a hidden message written after an archive brings the conversation back.\n- Archiving again still saves the aggregate and publishes nothing new. The save may bump the version even though nothing changed. I left it because it matches the other command handlers.\n- Archiving a conversation the caller doesn't read is an `ERROR` on the operation (`NotFound`), not a 4xx at request time, since that's how the other commands refuse.\n\n**Test results:** full Jest run, 271 suites and 1,665 tests, all passing. I didn't start a server, so nothing ran on port 4471; the e2e tests use their own ephemeral port.",
